{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CEMiA35Z3Jk43PisP4UcJA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/config.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Demo-application–facing configuration plumbing for quic-core:\n4\t//! the [`Config`] bag of CLI-derived options, the [`OptionId`]\n5\t//! tag identifying each option, and [`Config::create_and_configure`],\n6\t//! the one-shot constructor that turns a populated config into a\n7\t//! fully-wired [`Quic`].\n8\t//!\n9\t//! Phase 1: signatures only — every body is `todo!()`.\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Pointer-shape decisions for the config struct were guided by\n12\t//! reading `quic/config.c`:\n13\t//!\n14\t//! * Every `char const*` string field that\n15\t//!   `config_clear` `free`s is owned in C (allocated via\n16\t//!   `config_set_string_param`'s `malloc` + `memcpy`).  These map\n17\t//!   to `Option<String>`; `None` substitutes for the C `NULL`\n18\t//!   sentinel that all callers test before use.\n19\t//! * `multipath_alt_config: *mut char` is owned the same way and\n20\t//!   becomes `Option<String>`.\n21\t//! * `ech_target: uint8_t*` plus `ech_target_len` is owned by the\n22\t//!   config (`config_clear` frees it after the base64\n23\t//!   decode in `option_ECH_client`); it becomes\n24\t//!   `Option<Vec<u8>>` with the length implicit in the vector.\n25\t//! * `ticket_encryption_key: const uint8_t*` is *borrowed* in C —\n26\t//!   `config_clear` does not free it.  Phase 1 stores an\n27\t//!   owned `Option<Vec<u8>>` for safety; in v1 only the demo apps\n28\t//!   set this field, and they can supply an owned buffer.  Phase 3\n29\t//!   may revisit if a caller actually relies on aliasing.  The\n30\t//!   paired `ticket_encryption_key_length` field is dropped — its\n31\t//!   value is always implicit in the Vec length.\n32\t//! * Single-bit `unsigned int : 1` flag bitfields (`use_long_log`,\n33\t//!   `do_retry`, …) collapse to individual `bool` fields.  Every C\n34\t//!   call site reads/writes one bit at a time as a Boolean\n35\t//!   (`config->do_retry = 1`), so the\n36\t//!   integer-with-mask-and-shift translation buys nothing here and\n37\t//!   `bitflags!` is overkill for an unrelated set of flags.\n38\t//! * Bitfield `enable_sslkeylog` is gated by\n39\t//!   `#ifndef WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG` in C.  v1 follows the\n40\t//!   canonical build (the macro is undefined), so the field is\n41\t//!   always present in Rust; a `cfg`-gated variant lands when the\n42\t//!   build options are translated.\n43\t\n44\tuse crate::Error;\n45\tuse crate::Instant;\n46\tuse crate::internal::MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX;\n47\tuse crate::{LossbitVersion, Quic, SpinbitVersion, StreamDataCallback};\n48\t\n49\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n50\t// Option identifiers.\n51\t\n52\t/// One identifier per CLI / API option understood by [`Config`].\n53\t///\n54\t/// Mirrors the C `picoquic_option_enum_t`; variant order is\n55\t/// load-bearing — the option dispatch table in `quic/config.c`\n56\t/// indexes by variant — so the discriminants do not get reordered.\n57\t///\n58\t/// [`OptionId::SslKeyLog`] is unconditional here even though the C\n59\t/// enum gates it on `#ifndef WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG`, matching the\n60\t/// canonical-build behavior; see the module-level docs for the\n61\t/// rationale.\n62\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n63\tpub enum OptionId {\n64\t    Cert,\n65\t    Key,\n66\t    ServerPort,\n67\t    ProposedVersion,\n68\t    OutDir,\n69\t    WwwDir,\n70\t    MaxConnections,\n71\t    DoRetry,\n72\t    InitialRandom,\n73\t    ResetSeed,\n74\t    DisablePortBlocking,\n75\t    SolutionDir,\n76\t    CcAlgo,\n77\t    CcOption,\n78\t    Spinbit,\n79\t    Lossbit,\n80\t    Multipath,\n81\t    DestIf,\n82\t    CipherSuite,\n83\t    InitCnxId,\n84\t    LogFile,\n85\t    LongLog,\n86\t    BinlogDir,\n87\t    QlogDir,\n88\t    MtuMax,\n89\t    Sni,\n90\t    Alpn,\n91\t    RootTrustFile,\n92\t    ForceZeroShare,\n93\t    CnxIdLength,\n94\t    NoDisk,\n95\t    IdleTimeout,\n96\t    LargeClientHello,\n97\t    TicketFileName,\n98\t    TokenFileName,\n99\t    SocketBufferSize,\n100\t    PerformanceLog,\n101\t    PreemptiveRepeat,\n102\t    VersionUpgrade,\n103\t    NoGso,\n104\t    BdpFrame,\n105\t    CwinMax,\n106\t    SslKeyLog,\n107\t    AddressDiscovery,\n108\t    EchServer,\n109\t    EchClient,\n110\t    EchInit,\n111\t    FlowControlMax,\n112\t    PreferredV4,\n113\t    PreferredV6,\n114\t    Help,\n115\t}\n116\t\n117\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n118\t// Option table (mirrors C static option_table[]).\n119\t\n120\tstruct OptionEntry {\n121\t    id: OptionId,\n122\t    letter: char,\n123\t    name: &'static str,\n124\t    nb_params: usize,\n125\t    param_sample: &'static str,\n126\t    help: &'static str,\n127\t}\n128\t\n129\tstatic OPTION_TABLE: &[OptionEntry] = &[\n130\t    OptionEntry {\n131\t        id: OptionId::Cert,\n132\t        letter: 'c',\n133\t        name: \"cert\",\n134\t        nb_params: 1,\n135\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n136\t        help: \"cert file\",\n137\t    },\n138\t    OptionEntry {\n139\t        id: OptionId::Key,\n140\t        letter: 'k',\n141\t        name: \"key\",\n142\t        nb_params: 1,\n143\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n144\t        help: \"key file\",\n145\t    },\n146\t    OptionEntry {\n147\t        id: OptionId::ServerPort,\n148\t        letter: 'p',\n149\t        name: \"port\",\n150\t        nb_params: 1,\n151\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n152\t        help: \"server port\",\n153\t    },\n154\t    OptionEntry {\n155\t        id: OptionId::ProposedVersion,\n156\t        letter: 'v',\n157\t        name: \"proposed_version\",\n158\t        nb_params: 1,\n159\t        param_sample: \"\",\n160\t        help: \"Version proposed by client, e.g. -v ff000012\",\n161\t    },\n162\t    OptionEntry {\n163\t        id: OptionId::OutDir,\n164\t        letter: 'o',\n165\t        name: \"outdir\",\n166\t        nb_params: 1,\n167\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n168\t        help: \"Folder where client writes downloaded files, defaults to current directory.\",\n169\t    },\n170\t    OptionEntry {\n171\t        id: OptionId::WwwDir,\n172\t        letter: 'w',\n173\t        name: \"wwwdir\",\n174\t        nb_params: 1,\n175\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n176\t        help: \"Folder containing web pages served by server\",\n177\t    },\n178\t    OptionEntry {\n179\t        id: OptionId::MaxConnections,\n180\t        letter: 'x',\n181\t        name: \"max_connections\",\n182\t        nb_params: 1,\n183\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n184\t        help: \"Maximum number of concurrent connections, default 256\",\n185\t    },\n186\t    OptionEntry {\n187\t        id: OptionId::DoRetry,\n188\t        letter: 'r',\n189\t        name: \"do_retry\",\n190\t        nb_params: 0,\n191\t        param_sample: \"\",\n192\t        help: \"Do Retry Request\",\n193\t    },\n194\t    OptionEntry {\n195\t        id: OptionId::InitialRandom,\n196\t        letter: 'R',\n197\t        name: \"initial_random\",\n198\t        nb_params: 1,\n199\t        param_sample: \"option\",\n200\t        help: \"Randomize packet number spaces: none(0), initial(1, default), all(2).\",\n201\t    },\n202\t    OptionEntry {\n203\t        id: OptionId::ResetSeed,\n204\t        letter: 's',\n205\t        name: \"reset_seed\",\n206\t        nb_params: 1,\n207\t        param_sample: \"<32 hex chars>\",\n208\t        help: \"Reset seed\",\n209\t    },\n210\t    OptionEntry {\n211\t        id: OptionId::DisablePortBlocking,\n212\t        letter: 'X',\n213\t        name: \"disable_block\",\n214\t        nb_params: 0,\n215\t        param_sample: \"\",\n216\t        help: \"Disable the check for blocked ports\",\n217\t    },\n218\t    OptionEntry {\n219\t        id: OptionId::SolutionDir,\n220\t        letter: 'S',\n221\t        name: \"solution_dir\",\n222\t        nb_params: 1,\n223\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n224\t        help: \"Set the path to the source files to find the default files\",\n225\t    },\n226\t    OptionEntry {\n227\t        id: OptionId::CcAlgo,\n228\t        letter: 'G',\n229\t        name: \"cc_algo\",\n230\t        nb_params: 1,\n231\t        param_sample: \"cc_algorithm\",\n232\t        help: \"Use the specified congestion control algorithm. Defaults to bbr.\",\n233\t    },\n234\t    OptionEntry {\n235\t        id: OptionId::CcOption,\n236\t        letter: 'H',\n237\t        name: \"cco\",\n238\t        nb_params: 1,\n239\t        param_sample: \"option\",\n240\t        help: \"Set option string if required by congestion control algorithm.\",\n241\t    },\n242\t    OptionEntry {\n243\t        id: OptionId::Spinbit,\n244\t        letter: 'P',\n245\t        name: \"spinbit\",\n246\t        nb_params: 1,\n247\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n248\t        help: \"Set the default spinbit policy\",\n249\t    },\n250\t    OptionEntry {\n251\t        id: OptionId::Lossbit,\n252\t        letter: 'O',\n253\t        name: \"lossbit\",\n254\t        nb_params: 1,\n255\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n256\t        help: \"Set the default lossbit policy\",\n257\t    },\n258\t    OptionEntry {\n259\t        id: OptionId::Multipath,\n260\t        letter: 'M',\n261\t        name: \"multipath\",\n262\t        nb_params: 0,\n263\t        param_sample: \"\",\n264\t        help: \"Enable QUIC multipath extension\",\n265\t    },\n266\t    OptionEntry {\n267\t        id: OptionId::DestIf,\n268\t        letter: 'e',\n269\t        name: \"dest_if\",\n270\t        nb_params: 1,\n271\t        param_sample: \"if\",\n272\t        help: \"Send on interface (default: -1)\",\n273\t    },\n274\t    OptionEntry {\n275\t        id: OptionId::CipherSuite,\n276\t        letter: 'C',\n277\t        name: \"cipher_suite\",\n278\t        nb_params: 1,\n279\t        param_sample: \"cipher_suite_id\",\n280\t        help: \"specify cipher suite (e.g. -C 20 = chacha20)\",\n281\t    },\n282\t    OptionEntry {\n283\t        id: OptionId::InitCnxId,\n284\t        letter: 'i',\n285\t        name: \"cnxid_params\",\n286\t        nb_params: 1,\n287\t        param_sample: \"per-text-lb-spec\",\n288\t        help: \"See documentation for LB compatible CID configuration\",\n289\t    },\n290\t    OptionEntry {\n291\t        id: OptionId::LogFile,\n292\t        letter: 'l',\n293\t        name: \"text_log\",\n294\t        nb_params: 1,\n295\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n296\t        help: \"Log file, Log to stdout if file = \\\"-\\\". No text logging if absent.\",\n297\t    },\n298\t    OptionEntry {\n299\t        id: OptionId::LongLog,\n300\t        letter: 'L',\n301\t        name: \"long_log\",\n302\t        nb_params: 0,\n303\t        param_sample: \"\",\n304\t        help: \"Log all packets. If absent, log stops after 100 packets.\",\n305\t    },\n306\t    OptionEntry {\n307\t        id: OptionId::BinlogDir,\n308\t        letter: 'b',\n309\t        name: \"binlog_dir\",\n310\t        nb_params: 1,\n311\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n312\t        help: \"Binary logging to this directory. No binary logging if absent.\",\n313\t    },\n314\t    OptionEntry {\n315\t        id: OptionId::QlogDir,\n316\t        letter: 'q',\n317\t        name: \"qlog_dir\",\n318\t        nb_params: 1,\n319\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n320\t        help: \"Qlog logging to this directory.\",\n321\t    },\n322\t    OptionEntry {\n323\t        id: OptionId::MtuMax,\n324\t        letter: 'm',\n325\t        name: \"mtu_max\",\n326\t        nb_params: 1,\n327\t        param_sample: \"mtu_max\",\n328\t        help: \"Largest mtu value that can be tried for discovery.\",\n329\t    },\n330\t    OptionEntry {\n331\t        id: OptionId::Sni,\n332\t        letter: 'n',\n333\t        name: \"sni\",\n334\t        nb_params: 1,\n335\t        param_sample: \"sni\",\n336\t        help: \"sni (default: server name)\",\n337\t    },\n338\t    OptionEntry {\n339\t        id: OptionId::Alpn,\n340\t        letter: 'a',\n341\t        name: \"alpn\",\n342\t        nb_params: 1,\n343\t        param_sample: \"alpn\",\n344\t        help: \"alpn (default function of version)\",\n345\t    },\n346\t    OptionEntry {\n347\t        id: OptionId::RootTrustFile,\n348\t        letter: 't',\n349\t        name: \"root_trust_file\",\n350\t        nb_params: 1,\n351\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n352\t        help: \"root trust file\",\n353\t    },\n354\t    OptionEntry {\n355\t        id: OptionId::ForceZeroShare,\n356\t        letter: 'z',\n357\t        name: \"force_zero_share\",\n358\t        nb_params: 0,\n359\t        param_sample: \"\",\n360\t        help: \"Set TLS zero share behavior on client, to force HRR\",\n361\t    },\n362\t    OptionEntry {\n363\t        id: OptionId::CnxIdLength,\n364\t        letter: 'I',\n365\t        name: \"cnxid_length\",\n366\t        nb_params: 1,\n367\t        param_sample: \"length\",\n368\t        help: \"Length of CNX_ID used by the client, default=8\",\n369\t    },\n370\t    OptionEntry {\n371\t        id: OptionId::IdleTimeout,\n372\t        letter: 'd',\n373\t        name: \"idle_timeout\",\n374\t        nb_params: 1,\n375\t        param_sample: \"ms\",\n376\t        help: \"Duration of idle timeout in milliseconds (Default 30,000ms)\",\n377\t    },\n378\t    OptionEntry {\n379\t        id: OptionId::NoDisk,\n380\t        letter: 'D',\n381\t        name: \"no_disk\",\n382\t        nb_params: 0,\n383\t        param_sample: \"\",\n384\t        help: \"no disk: do not save received files on disk\",\n385\t    },\n386\t    OptionEntry {\n387\t        id: OptionId::LargeClientHello,\n388\t        letter: 'Q',\n389\t        name: \"large_client_hello\",\n390\t        nb_params: 0,\n391\t        param_sample: \"\",\n392\t        help: \"send a large client hello in order to test post quantum readiness\",\n393\t    },\n394\t    OptionEntry {\n395\t        id: OptionId::TicketFileName,\n396\t        letter: 'T',\n397\t        name: \"ticket_file\",\n398\t        nb_params: 1,\n399\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n400\t        help: \"File storing the session tickets\",\n401\t    },\n402\t    OptionEntry {\n403\t        id: OptionId::TokenFileName,\n404\t        letter: 'N',\n405\t        name: \"token_file\",\n406\t        nb_params: 1,\n407\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n408\t        help: \"File storing the new tokens\",\n409\t    },\n410\t    OptionEntry {\n411\t        id: OptionId::SocketBufferSize,\n412\t        letter: 'B',\n413\t        name: \"so_buf_size\",\n414\t        nb_params: 1,\n415\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n416\t        help: \"Set buffer size with SO_SNDBUF SO_RCVBUF\",\n417\t    },\n418\t    OptionEntry {\n419\t        id: OptionId::PerformanceLog,\n420\t        letter: 'F',\n421\t        name: \"log_file_name\",\n422\t        nb_params: 1,\n423\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n424\t        help: \"Append performance reports to performance log\",\n425\t    },\n426\t    OptionEntry {\n427\t        id: OptionId::PreemptiveRepeat,\n428\t        letter: 'V',\n429\t        name: \"preemptive_repeat\",\n430\t        nb_params: 0,\n431\t        param_sample: \"\",\n432\t        help: \"enable preemptive repeat\",\n433\t    },\n434\t    OptionEntry {\n435\t        id: OptionId::VersionUpgrade,\n436\t        letter: 'U',\n437\t        name: \"version_upgrade\",\n438\t        nb_params: 1,\n439\t        param_sample: \"\",\n440\t        help: \"Version upgrade if server agrees, e.g. -U 6b3343cf\",\n441\t    },\n442\t    OptionEntry {\n443\t        id: OptionId::NoGso,\n444\t        letter: '0',\n445\t        name: \"no_gso\",\n446\t        nb_params: 0,\n447\t        param_sample: \"\",\n448\t        help: \"Do not use UDP GSO or equivalent\",\n449\t    },\n450\t    OptionEntry {\n451\t        id: OptionId::BdpFrame,\n452\t        letter: 'j',\n453\t        name: \"bdp\",\n454\t        nb_params: 1,\n455\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n456\t        help: \"use bdp extension frame(1) or don't (0). Default=0\",\n457\t    },\n458\t    OptionEntry {\n459\t        id: OptionId::CwinMax,\n460\t        letter: 'W',\n461\t        name: \"cwin_max\",\n462\t        nb_params: 1,\n463\t        param_sample: \"bytes\",\n464\t        help: \"Max value for CWIN. Default=UINT64_MAX\",\n465\t    },\n466\t    OptionEntry {\n467\t        id: OptionId::SslKeyLog,\n468\t        letter: '8',\n469\t        name: \"sslkeylog\",\n470\t        nb_params: 0,\n471\t        param_sample: \"\",\n472\t        help: \"Enable SSLKEYLOG\",\n473\t    },\n474\t    OptionEntry {\n475\t        id: OptionId::AddressDiscovery,\n476\t        letter: 'J',\n477\t        name: \"addr_disc\",\n478\t        nb_params: 1,\n479\t        param_sample: \"mode\",\n480\t        help: \"provider (0), receiver (1) or both (2).\",\n481\t    },\n482\t    OptionEntry {\n483\t        id: OptionId::EchServer,\n484\t        letter: 'E',\n485\t        name: \"ech_s\",\n486\t        nb_params: 2,\n487\t        param_sample: \"key config\",\n488\t        help: \"ECH private key file, config file. Default= no ECH on server.\",\n489\t    },\n490\t    OptionEntry {\n491\t        id: OptionId::EchInit,\n492\t        letter: 'y',\n493\t        name: \"ech_init\",\n494\t        nb_params: 1,\n495\t        param_sample: \"public_name\",\n496\t        help: \"Create an ECH configuration before applying the `ech_s` parameter.\",\n497\t    },\n498\t    OptionEntry {\n499\t        id: OptionId::EchClient,\n500\t        letter: 'K',\n501\t        name: \"ech_c\",\n502\t        nb_params: 1,\n503\t        param_sample: \"base64\",\n504\t        help: \"ECH configuration for the client connection, base64 encoded.\",\n505\t    },\n506\t    OptionEntry {\n507\t        id: OptionId::FlowControlMax,\n508\t        letter: 'Z',\n509\t        name: \"flow_control_max\",\n510\t        nb_params: 1,\n511\t        param_sample: \"bytes\",\n512\t        help: \"Set the flow control's initial max data.\",\n513\t    },\n514\t    OptionEntry {\n515\t        id: OptionId::PreferredV4,\n516\t        letter: '4',\n517\t        name: \"preferred_v4\",\n518\t        nb_params: 1,\n519\t        param_sample: \"ip[:port]\",\n520\t        help: \"Preferred address for v4 connections.\",\n521\t    },\n522\t    OptionEntry {\n523\t        id: OptionId::PreferredV6,\n524\t        letter: '6',\n525\t        name: \"preferred_v6\",\n526\t        nb_params: 1,\n527\t        param_sample: \"ipv6[:port]\",\n528\t        help: \"Preferred address for v6 connections.\",\n529\t    },\n530\t    OptionEntry {\n531\t        id: OptionId::Help,\n532\t        letter: 'h',\n533\t        name: \"help\",\n534\t        nb_params: 0,\n535\t        param_sample: \"\",\n536\t        help: \"This help message\",\n537\t    },\n538\t];\n539\t\n540\tfn parse_hex_version(s: &str) -> u32 {\n541\t    u32::from_str_radix(s, 16).unwrap_or(0)\n542\t}\n543\t\n544\tfn option_entry(id: OptionId) -> Option<&'static OptionEntry> {\n545\t    OPTION_TABLE.iter().find(|e| e.id == id)\n546\t}\n547\t\n548\tfn option_entry_by_letter(letter: char) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n549\t    OPTION_TABLE\n550\t        .iter()\n551\t        .enumerate()\n552\t        .find(|(_, e)| e.letter == letter)\n553\t}\n554\t\n555\tfn option_entry_by_name(name: &str) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n556\t    OPTION_TABLE\n557\t        .iter()\n558\t        .enumerate()\n559\t        .find(|(_, e)| e.name == name)\n560\t}\n561\t\n562\tfn apply_option(config: &mut Config, entry: &OptionEntry, params: &[&str]) -> Result<(), Error> {\n563\t    let p0 = params.first().copied();\n564\t    let p1 = params.get(1).copied();\n565\t    match entry.id {\n566\t        OptionId::Cert => {\n567\t            config.server_cert_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n568\t        }\n569\t        OptionId::Key => {\n570\t            config.server_key_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n571\t        }\n572\t        OptionId::ServerPort => {\n573\t            config.set_port(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?)?;\n574\t        }\n575\t        OptionId::ProposedVersion => {\n576\t            let v = parse_hex_version(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n577\t            if v == 0 {\n578\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n579\t            }\n580\t            config.proposed_version = v;\n581\t        }\n582\t        OptionId::OutDir => {\n583\t            config.out_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n584\t        }\n585\t        OptionId::WwwDir => {\n586\t            config.www_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n587\t        }\n588\t        OptionId::MaxConnections => {\n589\t            let v: i32 = p0\n590\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n591\t                .parse()\n592\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n593\t            if v <= 0 {\n594\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n595\t            }\n596\t            config.nb_connections = v as u32;\n597\t        }\n598\t        OptionId::DoRetry => {\n599\t            config.do_retry = true;\n600\t        }\n601\t        OptionId::InitialRandom => {\n602\t            let v: i32 = p0\n603\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n604\t                .parse()\n605\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n606\t            if !(0..=2).contains(&v) {\n607\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n608\t            }\n609\t            config.initial_random = v as u32;\n610\t        }\n611\t        OptionId::ResetSeed => {\n612\t            config.has_reset_seed = true;\n613\t            let n =\n614\t                crate::utils::parse_hexa(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?, &mut config.reset_seed);\n615\t            if n != config.reset_seed.len() {\n616\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n617\t            }\n618\t        }\n619\t        OptionId::DisablePortBlocking => {\n620\t            config.disable_port_blocking = true;\n621\t        }\n622\t        OptionId::SslKeyLog => {\n623\t            config.enable_sslkeylog = true;\n624\t        }\n625\t        OptionId::SolutionDir => {\n626\t            config.solution_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n627\t        }\n628\t        OptionId::CcAlgo => {\n629\t            config.cc_algo_id = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n630\t        }\n631\t        OptionId::CcOption => {\n632\t            config.cc_algo_option_string = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n633\t        }\n634\t        OptionId::Spinbit => {\n635\t            let v: i32 = p0\n636\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n637\t                .parse()\n638\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n639\t            config.spinbit_policy = match v {\n640\t                0 => SpinbitVersion::Basic,\n641\t                1 => SpinbitVersion::Random,\n642\t                2 => SpinbitVersion::Null,\n643\t                3 => SpinbitVersion::On,\n644\t                _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n645\t            };\n646\t        }\n647\t        OptionId::Lossbit => {\n648\t            let v: i32 = p0\n649\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n650\t                .parse()\n651\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n652\t            config.lossbit_policy = match v {\n653\t                0 => LossbitVersion::None,\n654\t                1 => LossbitVersion::SendOnly,\n655\t                2 => LossbitVersion::SendReceive,\n656\t                _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n657\t            };\n658\t        }\n659\t        OptionId::Multipath => {\n660\t            config.multipath_option = 1;\n661\t        }\n662\t        OptionId::DestIf => {\n663\t            config.dest_if = p0\n664\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n665\t                .parse()\n666\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n667\t        }\n668\t        OptionId::CipherSuite => {\n669\t            config.cipher_suite_id = p0\n670\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n671\t                .parse()\n672\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n673\t        }\n674\t        OptionId::InitCnxId => {\n675\t            config.connection_id_cbdata = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n676\t        }\n677\t        OptionId::LogFile => {\n678\t            config.log_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n679\t        }\n680\t        OptionId::LongLog => {\n681\t            config.use_long_log = true;\n682\t        }\n683\t        OptionId::BinlogDir => {\n684\t            config.bin_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n685\t        }\n686\t        OptionId::QlogDir => {\n687\t            config.qlog_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n688\t        }\n689\t        OptionId::MtuMax => {\n690\t            let v: i32 = p0\n691\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n692\t                .parse()\n693\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n694\t            if v <= 0 {\n695\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n696\t            }\n697\t            config.mtu_max = v;\n698\t        }\n699\t        OptionId::Sni => {\n700\t            config.sni = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n701\t        }\n702\t        OptionId::Alpn => {\n703\t            config.alpn = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n704\t        }\n705\t        OptionId::RootTrustFile => {\n706\t            config.root_trust_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n707\t        }\n708\t        OptionId::ForceZeroShare => {\n709\t            config.force_zero_share = true;\n710\t        }\n711\t        OptionId::CnxIdLength => {\n712\t            let v: i32 = p0\n713\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n714\t                .parse()\n715\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n716\t            if v < 0 {\n717\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n718\t            }\n719\t            config.connection_id_length = v;\n720\t        }\n721\t        OptionId::IdleTimeout => {\n722\t            let v: i32 = p0\n723\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n724\t                .parse()\n725\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n726\t            if v < 0 {\n727\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n728\t            }\n729\t            config.idle_timeout = v;\n730\t        }\n731\t        OptionId::NoDisk => {\n732\t            config.no_disk = true;\n733\t        }\n734\t        OptionId::LargeClientHello => {\n735\t            config.large_client_hello = true;\n736\t        }\n737\t        OptionId::TicketFileName => {\n738\t            config.ticket_file_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n739\t        }\n740\t        OptionId::TokenFileName => {\n741\t            config.token_file_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n742\t        }\n743\t        OptionId::SocketBufferSize => {\n744\t            let v: i32 = p0\n745\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n746\t                .parse()\n747\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n748\t            if v < 0 {\n749\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n750\t            }\n751\t            config.socket_buffer_size = v;\n752\t        }\n753\t        OptionId::PerformanceLog => {\n754\t            config.performance_log = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n755\t        }\n756\t        OptionId::PreemptiveRepeat => {\n757\t            config.do_preemptive_repeat = true;\n758\t        }\n759\t        OptionId::VersionUpgrade => {\n760\t            let v = parse_hex_version(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n761\t            if v == 0 {\n762\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n763\t            }\n764\t            config.desired_version = v;\n765\t        }\n766\t        OptionId::NoGso => {\n767\t            config.do_not_use_gso = true;\n768\t        }\n769\t        OptionId::BdpFrame => {\n770\t            let v: i32 = p0\n771\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n772\t                .parse()\n773\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n774\t            if !(0..=1).contains(&v) {\n775\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n776\t            }\n777\t            config.bdp_frame_option = v;\n778\t        }\n779\t        OptionId::CwinMax => {\n780\t            let v: i64 = p0\n781\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n782\t                .parse()\n783\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n784\t            if v < 0 {\n785\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n786\t            }\n787\t            config.cwin_max = if v == 0 { u64::MAX } else { v as u64 };\n788\t        }\n789\t        OptionId::AddressDiscovery => {\n790\t            let v: i32 = p0\n791\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n792\t                .parse()\n793\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n794\t            if !(0..=2).contains(&v) {\n795\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n796\t            }\n797\t            config.address_discovery_mode = v + 1;\n798\t        }\n799\t        OptionId::EchServer => {\n800\t            config.ech_key_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n801\t            if let Some(s) = p1 {\n802\t                config.ech_config_file = Some(s.to_string());\n803\t            }\n804\t        }\n805\t        OptionId::EchInit => {\n806\t            config.ech_public_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n807\t        }\n808\t        OptionId::EchClient => {\n809\t            let s = p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n810\t            if s == \"-\" {\n811\t                config.ech_target = None;\n812\t            } else {\n813\t                todo!(\"EchClient base64 decode: picoquic_base64_decode not yet translated\")\n814\t            }\n815\t        }\n816\t        OptionId::FlowControlMax => {\n817\t            let v: i64 = p0\n818\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n819\t                .parse()\n820\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n821\t            if v < 0 {\n822\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n823\t            }\n824\t            config.flow_control_max = v as u64;\n825\t        }\n826\t        OptionId::PreferredV4 => {\n827\t            config.preferred_address_v4 = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n828\t        }\n829\t        OptionId::PreferredV6 => {\n830\t            config.preferred_address_v6 = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n831\t        }\n832\t        OptionId::Help => {\n833\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n834\t        }\n835\t    }\n836\t    Ok(())\n837\t}\n838\t\n839\tfn collect_params<'a>(\n840\t    entry: &OptionEntry,\n841\t    p_optind: &mut usize,\n842\t    argv: &[&'a str],\n843\t    optarg: Option<&'a str>,\n844\t) -> Result<Vec<&'a str>, Error> {\n845\t    let mut params = Vec::new();\n846\t    if entry.nb_params > 0 {\n847\t        params.push(optarg.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n848\t        let mut nb = 1;\n849\t        while nb < entry.nb_params {\n850\t            if *p_optind >= argv.len() {\n851\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n852\t            }\n853\t            params.push(argv[*p_optind]);\n854\t            *p_optind += 1;\n855\t            nb += 1;\n856\t        }\n857\t    }\n858\t    Ok(params)\n859\t}\n860\t\n861\tfn parse_option_string(opt_string: &str) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n862\t    if opt_string.starts_with(\"--\") && opt_string.len() > 2 {\n863\t        option_entry_by_name(&opt_string[2..])\n864\t    } else if opt_string.starts_with('-') && opt_string.len() == 2 {\n865\t        opt_string.chars().nth(1).and_then(option_entry_by_letter)\n866\t    } else {\n867\t        None\n868\t    }\n869\t}\n870\t\n871\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n872\t// Configuration struct.\n873\t\n874\t/// Configuration bag for a QUIC context, populated from CLI flags\n875\t/// (via [`Config::command_line`]) or directly (via\n876\t/// [`Config::set_option`]) and consumed by\n877\t/// [`Config::create_and_configure`].\n878\t///\n879\t/// Mirrors the C `picoquic_quic_config_t` field-for-field;\n880\t/// `repr(C)` is dropped because the struct never crosses an\n881\t/// external boundary.  See the module-level docs for the\n882\t/// pointer-shape rationale.\n883\t///\n884\t/// `Default` produces the documented C defaults:\n885\t/// `nb_connections = 256`, `connection_id_length = -1`, `cwin_max =\n886\t/// u64::MAX`, idle timeout from `MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX`, etc.  This\n887\t/// folds the C `picoquic_config_init` step into the constructor —\n888\t/// the C `config_clear` (which `free`s every owned string) collapses\n889\t/// to `Drop`, and resetting a config to defaults is just\n890\t/// `*config = Config::default()`.\n891\t#[derive(Debug)]\n892\tpub struct Config {\n893\t    pub nb_connections: u32,\n894\t    pub solution_dir: Option<String>,\n895\t    pub server_cert_file: Option<String>,\n896\t    pub server_key_file: Option<String>,\n897\t    pub log_file: Option<String>,\n898\t    pub bin_dir: Option<String>,\n899\t    pub qlog_dir: Option<String>,\n900\t    pub performance_log: Option<String>,\n901\t    pub server_port: u16,\n902\t    pub local_port: u16,\n903\t    /// Whether the public port is shared with sibling threads\n904\t    /// (`SO_REUSEPORT`).  C: `int is_port_shared`, used as a\n905\t    /// Boolean flag.\n906\t    pub is_port_shared: bool,\n907\t    pub nb_threads: i32,\n908\t    pub dest_if: i32,\n909\t    pub mtu_max: i32,\n910\t    /// `-1` is the C \"unset\" sentinel applied by [`Self::init`];\n911\t    /// values `>= 0` set the connection-ID length explicitly.  Kept\n912\t    /// as `i32` rather than `Option<u8>` for source-level parity\n913\t    /// with the C body.\n914\t    pub connection_id_length: i32,\n915\t    pub idle_timeout: i32,\n916\t    pub socket_buffer_size: i32,\n917\t    pub cc_algo_id: Option<String>,\n918\t    pub cc_algo_option_string: Option<String>,\n919\t    pub connection_id_cbdata: Option<String>,\n920\t    pub spinbit_policy: SpinbitVersion,\n921\t    pub lossbit_policy: LossbitVersion,\n922\t    pub multipath_option: i32,\n923\t    pub multipath_alt_config: Option<String>,\n924\t    pub bdp_frame_option: i32,\n925\t    pub cwin_max: u64,\n926\t    pub address_discovery_mode: i32,\n927\t\n928\t    // Common flags.\n929\t    pub initial_random: u32,\n930\t    pub use_long_log: bool,\n931\t    pub do_preemptive_repeat: bool,\n932\t    pub do_not_use_gso: bool,\n933\t    pub disable_port_blocking: bool,\n934\t    /// Originally bitfield-gated by `#ifndef\n935\t    /// WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG`; v1 follows the canonical build\n936\t    /// (always defined), so the field is unconditional here.\n937\t    pub enable_sslkeylog: bool,\n938\t\n939\t    // Server only.\n940\t    pub www_dir: Option<String>,\n941\t    pub reset_seed: [u8; 16],\n942\t    /// Borrowed in C (`config_clear` does not free it); owned\n943\t    /// `Vec<u8>` here for safety.  The C\n944\t    /// `ticket_encryption_key_length` field is dropped — its value\n945\t    /// is always `ticket_encryption_key.as_ref().map_or(0, Vec::len)`.\n946\t    pub ticket_encryption_key: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n947\t\n948\t    // Server flags.\n949\t    pub do_retry: bool,\n950\t    pub has_reset_seed: bool,\n951\t\n952\t    // Client only.\n953\t    pub ticket_file_name: Option<String>,\n954\t    pub token_file_name: Option<String>,\n955\t    pub sni: Option<String>,\n956\t    pub alpn: Option<String>,\n957\t    pub out_dir: Option<String>,\n958\t    pub root_trust_file: Option<String>,\n959\t    pub cipher_suite_id: i32,\n960\t    pub proposed_version: u32,\n961\t    pub desired_version: u32,\n962\t    pub force_zero_share: bool,\n963\t    pub no_disk: bool,\n964\t    pub large_client_hello: bool,\n965\t\n966\t    // ECH parameters for server.\n967\t    pub ech_key_file: Option<String>,\n968\t    pub ech_config_file: Option<String>,\n969\t    pub ech_public_name: Option<String>,\n970\t    /// ECH parameter for the client, base64-decoded.  Owned by\n971\t    /// the config — `config_clear` frees it in C.  The C\n972\t    /// `ech_target_len` field is dropped — its value is always\n973\t    /// `ech_target.as_ref().map_or(0, Vec::len)`.\n974\t    pub ech_target: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n975\t\n976\t    pub flow_control_max: u64,\n977\t\n978\t    // Preferred address, encoded as strings.\n979\t    pub preferred_address_v4: Option<String>,\n980\t    pub preferred_address_v6: Option<String>,\n981\t}\n982\t\n983\timpl Default for Config {\n984\t    /// Build a fresh config with the documented C defaults.  C:\n985\t    /// `picoquic_config_init` (which the C body invoked after a\n986\t    /// zero-initialising `memset`).\n987\t    fn default() -> Self {\n988\t        Config {\n989\t            nb_connections: 256,\n990\t            solution_dir: None,\n991\t            server_cert_file: None,\n992\t            server_key_file: None,\n993\t            log_file: None,\n994\t            bin_dir: None,\n995\t            qlog_dir: None,\n996\t            performance_log: None,\n997\t            server_port: 0,\n998\t            local_port: 0,\n999\t            is_port_shared: false,\n1000\t            nb_threads: 0,\n1001\t            dest_if: 0,\n1002\t            mtu_max: 0,\n1003\t            connection_id_length: -1,\n1004\t            idle_timeout: (MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX.ticks() / 1000) as i32,\n1005\t            socket_buffer_size: 0,\n1006\t            cc_algo_id: None,\n1007\t            cc_algo_option_string: None,\n1008\t            connection_id_cbdata: None,\n1009\t            spinbit_policy: SpinbitVersion::default(),\n1010\t            lossbit_policy: LossbitVersion::default(),\n1011\t            multipath_option: 0,\n1012\t            multipath_alt_config: None,\n1013\t            bdp_frame_option: 0,\n1014\t            cwin_max: u64::MAX,\n1015\t            address_discovery_mode: 0,\n1016\t            initial_random: 3,\n1017\t            use_long_log: false,\n1018\t            do_preemptive_repeat: false,\n1019\t            do_not_use_gso: false,\n1020\t            disable_port_blocking: false,\n1021\t            enable_sslkeylog: false,\n1022\t            www_dir: None,\n1023\t            reset_seed: [0; 16],\n1024\t            ticket_encryption_key: None,\n1025\t            do_retry: false,\n1026\t            has_reset_seed: false,\n1027\t            ticket_file_name: None,\n1028\t            token_file_name: None,\n1029\t            sni: None,\n1030\t            alpn: None,\n1031\t            out_dir: None,\n1032\t            root_trust_file: None,\n1033\t            cipher_suite_id: 0,\n1034\t            proposed_version: 0,\n1035\t            desired_version: 0,\n1036\t            force_zero_share: false,\n1037\t            no_disk: false,\n1038\t            large_client_hello: false,\n1039\t            ech_key_file: None,\n1040\t            ech_config_file: None,\n1041\t            ech_public_name: None,\n1042\t            ech_target: None,\n1043\t            flow_control_max: 0,\n1044\t            preferred_address_v4: None,\n1045\t            preferred_address_v6: None,\n1046\t        }\n1047\t    }\n1048\t}\n1049\t\n1050\timpl Config {\n1051\t    /// Apply one option, selected by `option`, to the config.\n1052\t    /// C: `picoquic_config_set_option`.\n1053\t    ///\n1054\t    /// `value` is optional — flag-style options ([`OptionId::DoRetry`],\n1055\t    /// [`OptionId::LongLog`], …) ignore it; value-style options\n1056\t    /// require it and return `Err` when it is missing or malformed.\n1057\t    ///\n1058\t    /// The C signature returned `int` (`0` ↔ `Ok`, `-1` ↔ `Err`);\n1059\t    /// mapped to `Result<(), Error>`.\n1060\t    pub fn set_option(&mut self, option: OptionId, value: Option<&str>) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1061\t        let entry = option_entry(option).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n1062\t        let params: &[&str] = match value {\n1063\t            Some(v) => &[v],\n1064\t            None => &[],\n1065\t        };\n1066\t        apply_option(self, entry, params)\n1067\t    }\n1068\t\n1069\t    /// Dispatch one option from a single-character flag (`-x`).\n1070\t    /// C: `picoquic_config_command_line`.\n1071\t    ///\n1072\t    /// `p_optind` advances past any extra arguments consumed beyond\n1073\t    /// the inline `optarg`, mirroring the C in/out parameter so that\n1074\t    /// an outer getopt-style loop stays in sync.\n1075\t    ///\n1076\t    /// `argv` is a borrowed slice of borrowed strings — the C caller\n1077\t    /// (`first` etc.) owns the argument vector for the program\n1078\t    /// lifetime, so a borrow is safe.  The C `int argc` parameter is\n1079\t    /// dropped (implicit in `argv.len()`).\n1080\t    pub fn command_line(\n1081\t        &mut self,\n1082\t        opt: char,\n1083\t        p_optind: &mut usize,\n1084\t        argv: &[&str],\n1085\t        optarg: Option<&str>,\n1086\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1087\t        let (_, entry) = option_entry_by_letter(opt).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n1088\t        let params = collect_params(entry, p_optind, argv, optarg)?;\n1089\t        apply_option(self, entry, &params)\n1090\t    }\n1091\t\n1092\t    /// Like [`Self::command_line`] but accepts both single-character\n1093\t    /// (`-x`) and long-form (`--name`) option strings; the leading\n1094\t    /// dashes are part of `opt_string`, matching the C contract.\n1095\t    /// C: `picoquic_config_command_line_ex`.\n1096\t    pub fn command_line_ex(\n1097\t        &mut self,\n1098\t        opt_string: &str,\n1099\t        p_optind: &mut usize,\n1100\t        argv: &[&str],\n1101\t        optarg: Option<&str>,\n1102\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1103\t        let (_, entry) = parse_option_string(opt_string).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n1104\t        let params = collect_params(entry, p_optind, argv, optarg)?;\n1105\t        apply_option(self, entry, &params)\n1106\t    }\n1107\t\n1108\t    /// Build the getopt-style option string from the dispatch table\n1109\t    /// in `config.c` — one letter per option, with `:` after each\n1110\t    /// option that takes an argument.  C:\n1111\t    /// `picoquic_config_option_letters`.\n1112\t    ///\n1113\t    /// The C signature wrote into a caller-supplied buffer\n1114\t    /// (`option_string`, `string_max`) and reported the populated\n1115\t    /// length via `*string_length`.  The Rust wrapper owns the\n1116\t    /// buffer and returns it directly, so the buffer-too-small\n1117\t    /// failure mode disappears.\n1118\t    pub fn option_letters() -> String {\n1119\t        let mut s = String::new();\n1120\t        for e in OPTION_TABLE {\n1121\t            s.push(e.letter);\n1122\t            if e.nb_params > 0 {\n1123\t                s.push(':');\n1124\t            }\n1125\t        }\n1126\t        s\n1127\t    }\n1128\t\n1129\t    /// Write the option help to a [`core::fmt::Write`] sink.\n1130\t    /// C: `picoquic_config_usage_file`.\n1131\t    ///\n1132\t    /// The C parameter was `FILE*`; the Rust translation accepts\n1133\t    /// any sink (a `String` buffer, the stdout/stderr handles under\n1134\t    /// the `std` feature, or a custom writer) so the function\n1135\t    /// stays `no_std`-friendly.\n1136\t    pub fn write_usage(w: &mut dyn core::fmt::Write) {\n1137\t        let _ = w.write_str(\"Picoquic options:\\n\");\n1138\t        for e in OPTION_TABLE {\n1139\t            let _ = write!(w, \"  -{} {}\", e.letter, e.param_sample);\n1140\t            let pad = 12usize.saturating_sub(e.param_sample.len());\n1141\t            for _ in 0..pad {\n1142\t                let _ = w.write_char(' ');\n1143\t            }\n1144\t            let _ = writeln!(w, \" {}\", e.help);\n1145\t        }\n1146\t    }\n1147\t\n1148\t    /// Print the option help to stderr.  C: `picoquic_config_usage`.\n1149\t    ///\n1150\t    /// Phase 3 will route this through `eprintln!` (std-only); for\n1151\t    /// now it is just a `todo!()`.\n1152\t    pub fn print_usage() {\n1153\t        let mut buf = String::new();\n1154\t        Self::write_usage(&mut buf);\n1155\t        eprint!(\"{}\", buf);\n1156\t    }\n1157\t\n1158\t    /// Parse a port-configuration string into `server_port`,\n1159\t    /// `local_port`, `is_port_shared`, and `nb_threads`.\n1160\t    /// C: `config_set_port` (internal, called from the `-p` option\n1161\t    /// handler in `picoquic/config.c`).\n1162\t    ///\n1163\t    /// Accepted formats:\n1164\t    /// - `\"\"` / `\"0\"` — clear all (port 0, not shared)\n1165\t    /// - `\"4433\"` — server port only\n1166\t    /// - `\"443:4434\"` — server:local\n1167\t    /// - `\"S4433\"` — shared server port\n1168\t    /// - `\"S443:4434*256\"` — shared server:local, 256 threads\n1169\t    /// - `\"4433*7\"` — server port, 7 threads\n1170\t    ///\n1171\t    /// Returns `Err` when any token cannot be parsed or a port value\n1172\t    /// exceeds 65535.\n1173\t    pub fn set_port(&mut self, port_string: &str) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1174\t        let bytes = port_string.as_bytes();\n1175\t        let mut i = 0;\n1176\t        let mut is_port_shared = false;\n1177\t        let mut p1: i32 = 0;\n1178\t        let mut p2: i32 = 0;\n1179\t        let mut nb_threads: i32 = 0;\n1180\t\n1181\t        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b'S' {\n1182\t            is_port_shared = true;\n1183\t            i += 1;\n1184\t        }\n1185\t        while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n1186\t            p1 = p1 * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n1187\t            i += 1;\n1188\t        }\n1189\t        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b':' {\n1190\t            i += 1;\n1191\t            while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n1192\t                p2 = p2 * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n1193\t                i += 1;\n1194\t            }\n1195\t        }\n1196\t        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b'*' {\n1197\t            i += 1;\n1198\t            while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n1199\t                nb_threads = nb_threads * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n1200\t                i += 1;\n1201\t            }\n1202\t        }\n1203\t        if i != bytes.len() || !(0..=65535).contains(&p1) || !(0..=65535).contains(&p2) {\n1204\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n1205\t        }\n1206\t        self.server_port = p1 as u16;\n1207\t        self.local_port = p2 as u16;\n1208\t        self.is_port_shared = is_port_shared;\n1209\t        self.nb_threads = nb_threads;\n1210\t        Ok(())\n1211\t    }\n1212\t\n1213\t    /// Build a fully-configured QUIC context from this config plus\n1214\t    /// an application-supplied callback.  C:\n1215\t    /// `picoquic_create_and_configure`.\n1216\t    ///\n1217\t    /// Returns `None` when context creation fails (the C side\n1218\t    /// returned `NULL`).\n1219\t    ///\n1220\t    /// Pointer-shape choices, derived from the C signature and the\n1221\t    /// body in `config.c`:\n1222\t    ///\n1223\t    /// * `picoquic_quic_config_t* config` is consumed-borrowed\n1224\t    ///   (`&mut self`): the body reads every field and may set up\n1225\t    ///   downstream owned state, but it does not free the struct\n1226\t    ///   itself — ownership stays with the caller.\n1227\t    /// * `default_callback_fn` + `default_callback_ctx` collapse to\n1228\t    ///   one